## Model card

- **Name:** MAI Code 1 Flash
- **Short description:** Microsoft's MAI-Code-1-Flash, released June 2026; coding-optimized model; text input, text output; proprietary (weights not public).
- **Provider / access:** Microsoft API (`mai-code-1-flash`, Chat Completions); available via OpenCode.
- **Release / knowledge:** Released June 2026; knowledge cutoff Dec 2025.
- **IDs:** `mai-code-1-flash` (Microsoft API, OpenCode). No Free ID confirmed on OpenCode Zen.
- **Context window:** 256,000 tokens declared (opencode.ai); max output 128K tokens; no public long-context retrieval score.
- **Modalities:** Text in; text out; no vision/audio confirmed; tool calling not explicitly advertised; structured output/JSON not confirmed.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-20):** Not published on OpenCode (no efficiency data, no usage rows); treat as paid API, no Free tier confirmed.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary (parameter count not disclosed); coding-optimized; from Microsoft.

### Raw benchmarks found

No standardized benchmark scores found in any source checked. opencode.ai shows no usage rows and no efficiency data. No GPQA, HLE, MMLU, SWE-bench, LiveCodeBench, HumanEval, or any other public benchmark results exist.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

All quality dimensions and Overall are marked insufficient evidence; no numeric scores are assigned.

- **Tool use: insufficient evidence.** No public agent/tool benchmarks.
- **Reasoning: insufficient evidence.** No public reasoning benchmarks.
- **Context window: insufficient evidence.** Declared 256K tokens; no public retrieval score.
- **Multimodal: insufficient evidence.** Text in, text out only confirmed; no vision benchmark scores.
- **Coding: insufficient evidence.** No public coding benchmarks.
- **Cost efficiency: not scored** (per formula).
- **Overall Score: not computed — insufficient evidence.** No dimensional scores available to average.

